_url":"https://github.com/fpliger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fpliger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-14T18:50:13Z","updated_at":"2015-02-14T18:50:13Z","body":"what about no shipping test data and add hooks to lazily download it the first time it's needed (on tests and server)? \n\nIt may not be a good idea if this data is needed in serveral other places....\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74387063/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74391478","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890#issuecomment-74391478","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890","id":74391478,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0MzkxNDc4","user":{"login":"hhuuggoo","id":249407,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0OTQwNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249407?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo","html_url":"https://github.com/hhuuggoo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhuuggoo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-14T20:51:51Z","updated_at":"2015-02-14T20:53:44Z","body":"why is 13mb a big deal? is that size a barrier to people?  The default configuration for the blaze part of the bokeh server is a dummy configuration that makes all our examples and tests work.  The reason why the bokeh server isn't breaking for most people is that most people don't have all the blaze dependencies installed - therefore the blaze config isn't loaded.  I'm not sure what we want to do here, there are many options, I could also put try/excepts in the config so that we don't fail if we can't find the dataset (of course that means that tests and some examples won't work)\n\nWe can also decrease the size of the datafile by doing some downsampling - of course the AR examples will be less interesting if we do that\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74391478/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74392258","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890#issuecomment-74392258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890","id":74392258,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0MzkyMjU4","user":{"login":"almarklein","id":3015475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTU0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3015475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein","html_url":"https://github.com/almarklein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almarklein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-14T21:15:58Z","updated_at":"2015-02-14T21:15:58Z","body":"> what about no shipping test data and add hooks to lazily download it the\n> first time it's needed (on tests and server)?\n\nI have good experience with that with other packages. It's also an \napproach that scales nicely as you add more data.\n\nPersonally I prefer to keep _any_ data out of a main code repository \nexcept if its small and very much static. An auto-download approach \nallows you to put the data in its own repository.\n- Almar\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74392258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/74394789","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890#issuecomment-74394789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/1890","id":74394789,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0Mzk0Nzg5","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id"